# BRIEF B1520 | SEAT-M123: MPS CALCULATOR, BUILDER (SONNET): PIN THE .NET SDK EXACTLY IN CI, SO THE HOSTED RUNNER CAN NO LONGER MOVE THE BUILD TOOL UNDER US. NEW BRANCH `b1520/mps-sdk-exact-pin` FROM MAIN, ONE COMMIT, ONE PLAIN PUSH, NO PR. NOT MERGED, NOT DEPLOYED.

**Authority:** the product owner's 2026-11-11 19:52 ruling (pin the build tool exactly): "a small change in both repos so CI installs one exact .NET build tool; reds stop arriving by surprise, but each .NET update then needs its own pull request." Model: claude-sonnet-5-5 (`/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/TUESDAY/0_Brain/dashboard/data/models_latest.json`, the `sonnet` entry; `/usr/bin/grep -c 'claude-sonnet-5-5'` printed 2, at lines 23 and 38, MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER), row C2 at `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/specs/model-routing.md:92` (Sonnet 1st). **Launch carries `BRIEF_SEAT_LEVEL=sonnet` inside the quotes** (`brief_seat.sh` defaults to Opus). Gate after: a separate kit, tier G2 (config and CI). The ticket this serves is MPSCALC-387, whose fix shape 2 ("pin the SDK exactly in the workflow, or set rollForward to disable in global.json") is what was ruled; the key is named only in the PR HOOK section of your STATUS, never in a commit.

**BLUF (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER, hosted job logs read with `gh api --allow-escape-sequences -X GET repos/datasecau/MPS-Commercial-Calculator/actions/jobs/<id>/logs` under the project's `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, saved at `/private/tmp/b1519-drafter/mps_old_dotnet.log`, `mps_new_dotnet.log` and `mps_new_pkg.log`):** main's green `dotnet` job of 2026-11-10 (run 42761547464, main `54ed7627`, job 129648145803) logged runtime `10.0.14` "already installed" (line 160) and `dotnet-install: .NET Core SDK with version '10.0.403' is already installed` (line 162). Main's newest green run (run 42988098286, main `9a0c4ba8`, 2026-11-11 08:34Z): job `dotnet` 130414031404 logged `Installed version is 10.0.15` (line 165) and `Installed version is 10.0.404` (line 176); job `package` 130416745896 the same (lines 167 and 178). **The SDK moved from 10.0.403 to 10.0.404 between two green runs with no commit of ours**, and the publish-output tripwires turned every pull request red until the Pkcs pin was raised to 10.0.15 (#177). `global.json` is `{"version": "10.0.100", "rollForward": "latestFeature"}` (`global.json:3-4`): 10.0.100 is a floor so loose it is a feature band below what CI installs. **Both** `actions/setup-dotnet` steps (`ci.yml:38-40` job `dotnet` :30, `ci.yml:118-120` job `package` :109) take `global-json-file: global.json` and nothing else.

**THE SHAPE (recommended; Stamp slot SHAPE, default `A`): change `global.json` to `{"version": "10.0.404", "rollForward": "disable"}` and change NO workflow line.** Why this is exact and needs no workflow edit (DERIVED-BY-DRAFTER from `actions/setup-dotnet` at the pinned sha `a98b56852c35b8e3190ac28c8c2271da59106c68`, `src/setup-dotnet.ts:203-250`, read with `gh api -X GET repos/actions/setup-dotnet/contents/src/setup-dotnet.ts?ref=<sha>` raw): the action reads `sdk.version` from the file and, **only when `rollForward` is `latestMajor`, `latestMinor`, `latestFeature` or `latestPatch`, widens it** (`latestFeature` -> `10.0`, which is why the log shows `--channel 10.0`); for `disable` (or an absent key) no `case` fires and the version stays `10.0.404`, so the install script runs with `--version 10.0.404`. With `disable` the `dotnet` muxer refuses any SDK that is not exactly 10.0.404, so a newer SDK that the runner image already carries cannot be picked. Shape B (workflow-only) is a Stamp Q; the drafter does not recommend it and measured why.

## DESIGN ANSWERS (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER unless marked; you re-measure each in Step 1 and print it)
1. **global.json and setup-dotnet.** `global.json` at main: version `10.0.100`, rollForward `latestFeature` (blob read from `gh api -X GET repos/datasecau/MPS-Commercial-Calculator/contents/global.json?ref=aae420ff8a9e3f8a34be0aff22f8934e1708911a`). `.github/workflows/` holds one file, `ci.yml` (139 lines). `/usr/bin/grep -c -i 'setup-dotnet@'` = 2 (control: `-c 'actions/checkout@'` differs); both use `global-json-file: global.json`, neither `dotnet-version`. Job scan (`/private/tmp/b1519-drafter/jobscan.py`, control: job `dotnet` shows 2 `dotnet` commands): `dotnet` commands are written in job `dotnet` (`:42` build, `:43` test); job `package` has a `setup-dotnet` step (`:118`) and runs `bash scripts/package.sh` (`:128-130`), whose `dotnet publish` is inside the script (`scripts/package.sh:48`, printed `== dotnet publish src/MpsCalc.Api -c Release`): **a job that only calls a script still needs the pin, so the guard cannot find "jobs that run dotnet" by regex; it pins the CLOSED SET of jobs with a `setup-dotnet` step to `{dotnet, package}`**. Jobs `web` (:45) and `python` (:84) have none.
2. **The SDK the last green hosted runs installed.** Newest green main run: SDK **10.0.404**, runtime **10.0.15** (lines above). Last green main run before the drift: SDK **10.0.403**, runtime **10.0.14**, "already installed" on the image. Official metadata (`https://builds.dotnet.microsoft.com/dotnet/release-metadata/10.0/releases.json`, read once by the drafter): release 10.0.15 = SDK 10.0.404 = runtime 10.0.15 = ASP.NET Core 10.0.15, dated 2026-11-10; release 10.0.14 = SDK 10.0.403, dated 2026-10-25. **The SDK to pin is 10.0.404:** the one CI installs today and the one whose framework the Pkcs 10.0.15 pin matches.
3. **The project-local SDK and what the pin does to it.** `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/Datasec MPS Commercial Calculator/.tools/dotnet/dotnet --version` printed `10.0.401`; `.tools/dotnet/sdk` holds only `10.0.401`; shared frameworks `10.0.12`; the ASP.NET Core reference pack `10.0.12`. The project has no `.tools/env.sh`; seats put `.tools/dotnet` on PATH. **With `rollForward: disable` and version 10.0.404 every local `dotnet` command in a tree with the new `global.json` refuses until 10.0.404 is installed.** The two ways:
   - **A (recommended): global.json only, plus a local SDK 10.0.404 installed as a NAMED STEP in a SIDE DIRECTORY** (`.tools/dotnet-10.0.404`, never into `.tools/dotnet`: four live seats build with `.tools/dotnet`, and every older branch's `global.json` says `latestFeature`, so a newer SDK dropped into the shared directory would become theirs mid-flight). Download checksum from the official release metadata: file `https://builds.dotnet.microsoft.com/dotnet/Sdk/10.0.404/dotnet-sdk-10.0.404-osx-arm64.tar.gz`, **sha512 `1c9a13f625d0c08f08ef5a53597bababe3d2473527e98db2199210940c69dd5fc599a39a4d7c30ebf297ca2334a81b2f64b9bf05ff99585de9af4a5d85215e96`** (the `hash` field of the `osx-arm64` file of SDK 10.0.404 in `releases.json`; control: SDK 10.0.403's file prints a different hash). This machine is `arm64` (`uname -m`). Repository diff: `global.json` (2 lines), one new test file, one doc line. No workflow line.
   - **B: workflow only.** `dotnet-version: 10.0.404` in both `setup-dotnet` steps, `global.json` unchanged (local builds unaffected, which is why it looks smaller on this machine). It is NOT exact: a runner image that later carries a higher 10.0.4xx would still be selected by `latestFeature` (DERIVED). The CI-reader test `scripts/tests/test_ci_workflow.py` has no setup-dotnet row (86 lines, MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER), so B would not break it; B is rejected for exactness, not for a test.
4. **Does the Pkcs pin move with the SDK pin?** No. SDK 10.0.404 bundles ASP.NET Core 10.0.15 whose Pkcs file version is `10.0.1526.53008`, equal to package 10.0.15's (RELAYED: gate verdict `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/tuesday/briefs/2026-11-11_B1508_verify/VERDICT.md` checks 4 and 5). The pin is `src/MpsCalc.Api/MpsCalc.Api.csproj:28` (`Version="10.0.15"`), its comment `:32` already reads "(SDK 10.0.404 = 10.0.15)", the rank target `:37`: **all stay**. The test project's `System.Security.Cryptography.Xml` 10.0.13 is not Pkcs and does not move. Tripwires: `tests/MpsCalc.Api.Tests/PublishOutputTests.cs:96` (`B160_the_publish_output_carries_the_patched_pkcs_and_lists_it_in_deps_json`) and its control row; after the SDK is exact they can only turn red in a pull request that changes `global.json`, which is the ruling's "each .NET update needs its own pull request". **Tests that read `ci.yml` or `global.json`:** `scripts/tests/test_ci_workflow.py` reads `ci.yml` (jobs `["dotnet","web","python","package"]`, SHA-pinned actions, permissions); **no test reads `global.json`** (the commission named `infra/tests/test_ci_workflow.py`: there is none in this repository; `infra/tests/` holds `test_infra.py` only; the CI-reader is in `scripts/tests/`). Under A none of its lines changes.
5. **The red-first row.** A NEW file `scripts/tests/test_sdk_pin.py` (standard library only; the `python` job loops `tools/demo/test/test_*.py infra/tests/test_*.py scripts/tests/test_*.py` under `python3 -I`, `ci.yml:102-104`, "one failing file fails the step", so it runs with no workflow edit). It reads `global.json` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and fails when: `rollForward` is anything but `disable`; `version` is not a full `A.B.CDD` SDK version; any `setup-dotnet` step carries a `dotnet-version`, `dotnet-channel`, `dotnet-quality` or `source-url` key or lacks `global-json-file: global.json`; the set of jobs with a `setup-dotnet` step is not exactly `{dotnet, package}`. It is RED at main as it stands (`latestFeature`), GREEN after the pin, and red-proved on planted copies (Step 3).

**Limit, named and not fixed:** `actions/setup-dotnet` always runs a first install `--runtime dotnet --channel LTS` (`src/installer.ts:413-424`; hosted log lines 159 and 165), so the shared **Microsoft.NETCore.App** runtime still floats (10.0.15 today). The ASP.NET Core framework and targeting pack, which the Pkcs tripwires read, come from the exact SDK. Whether a newer NETCore.App alone can ever matter is UNMEASURED; write it in STATUS FOR TUESDAY, do nothing about it.

