At most TWO heavy jobs machine-wide across all MPS lanes. A heavy job here: the extraction, the first Release build, each whole `dotnet test` run (base once, head once), the package run. Take a slot by atomic `mkdir '<project>/.tools/.heavy-lock-1'` (else `-2`; neither free: poll every 60 s), write `holder.txt` (pane name, label, `date`), run ONE job, MOVE the holder file to `.tools/b1520/logs/`, `rmdir` your own dir; never touch another seat's holder (a holder older than 30 minutes with no live pane is REPORTED, never removed). **At drafting BOTH slots existed** (`ls -d` printed both, holders written 19:56, MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER; control: `.tools` lists 300 entries): expect to wait, and budget for it. Load gate: `LC_ALL=C uptime` load1 under 24 on TWO reads 120 s apart (not independent: say so; the drafter read 10.94 at 20:01). Single-file runs, plants and the Python files are light. A wait is not a finding; at the hard stop `BLOCKED: heavy lock waiting at load <n>`. Moved main: as Step 6.

